  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The landscape is a huge plain similar to northern plains, with mounds and slopes in elegant lines like a stream of jade green, and a tower every eight li holding wild Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        548
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_wild_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Daytime is a dazzling golden day; at night the sky is not fully dark, and silver light shines instead.",
      "chapters": [
        549
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Speaking to Ge tribe, Fang Yuan urges migration north and reliance on Huang Jin tribe. Ge tribe leader answers that the struggle in the imperial court is not something small clans can join.",
      "chapters": [
        440
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ge_tribe",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): chapter 440’s wording is Wang Ting blessed land. The novel text does not print an “also known as” line tying that name to other English aliases collected on this page.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan asks for information about Eighty-Eight True Yang Building in Imperial Court blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        487
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "imperial-court-naming",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "loc_imperial_court_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ma Ying Jie calls Imperial Court blessed land Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s grace left to his descendants, especially Eighty Eight True Yang Building with the Immortal Venerable’s inheritance. He adds that many other inheritances lie across the land, and that tribes who enter through history gain huge strength. Narration states setting up inheritances there has become a northern plains tradition, and that a fated person must first enter the blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        489
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritances-and-giant-suns-grace",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ma_ying_jie",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration calls Imperial Court blessed land northern plains’ greatest utopia, opening every ten years as a reward to the lord of northern plains. Entrants who step through the same gate are separated and randomly transported across the land. Mortal Gu use is not restricted inside; Immortal Gu cannot be restrained in any blessed land. The landscape is a huge plain similar to northern plains, with a tower every eight li holding wild Gu. When the Imperial Court contest first started, some Gu Masters tried to steal or attack those towers; they melted like candles until only white bone skeleton remained, smashed into a pile. Fang Yuan recalls that a nameless space path Gu Immortal created the huge land, that Giant Sun inherited it before becoming immortal, and that after becoming Immortal Venerable he set up the Imperial Court contest so the ancient blessed land continues, no longer suffering heavenly tribulations or earthly calamities under his manipulation. The land holds countless Gu Master inheritances.",
      "chapters": [
        548
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "landscape-and-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_mortal_gu",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "evt_arc_imperial_court_contest",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imperial Court blessed land is not safe; it holds large numbers of wild Gu worms and vicious beasts. It has much greater foundation than Hu Immortal Blessed Land, including weather changes and morning and night, and already has grotto-heaven traits as a quasi grotto-heaven. Daytime is dazzling gold; night is silver light rather than full dark. Narration calls it the largest blessed land in northern plains and a true land of treasures, where even rare azure wolves are common.",
      "chapters": [
        549
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "scale-and-wildlife",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    }
  ],
